{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Escape_Plan","to":"Escape Plan"},{"from":"Corpse_Explosion","to":"Corpse Explosion"},{"from":"Crippling_Cloud","to":"Crippling Cloud"},{"from":"After_Image","to":"After Image"},{"from":"Sneaky_Strike","to":"Sneaky Strike"},{"from":"Iron_Wave","to":"Iron Wave"},{"from":"Flash_of_Steel","to":"Flash of Steel"},{"from":"Leg_Sweep","to":"Leg Sweep"}],"pages":{"1319":{"pageid":1319,"ns":0,"title":"After Image","revisions":[{"revid":56610,"parentid":56306,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = After Image\n| Image       = Green-AfterImage.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. <br>)Whenever you play a card, gain 1 {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = After Image, Innate\n| PowerGives = Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = After Image\n| Image        = Icon AfterImage.png\n| Description  = Whenever you play a card, gain X {{KW|Block}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          =\n| GivesToPlayer = After Image, Block\n}}\n{{C|After Image}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|After Image}}, which gives {{KW|Block}} for every card played. If upgraded, it has {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|After Image}} will not be triggered by the {{C|After Image}} it came from.\n* {{BD|After Image}} takes effect ''before'' {{M|Corrupt Heart}}'s {{BD|Beat of Death}}. \n** With one {{BD|After Image}}, the initial {{BD|Beat of Death}} will be completely nullified below {{Asc|19}}. Above {{Asc|19}} it will be halved, or nullified in combination with {{R|Tungsten Rod}} or another {{BD|After Image}}.\n\n* {{BD|After Image}} takes effect ''before'' {{BD|Sharp Hide}} or {{BD|Thorns}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|After Image}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 11: A Library of Features'''\n** Curses/Statuses that play themselves no longer trigger Powers (Time Warp, After Image, etc)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** After Image card's large portrait now renders.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** AfterImage now works when playing Curse/Status cards via Medical Kit and Blue Candle.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2129":{"pageid":2129,"ns":0,"title":"Aggregate","revisions":[{"revid":56308,"parentid":53379,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Aggregate\n| Image       = Blue-Aggregate.png\n| Color       = Blue\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain {{Icon|BE}} for every (4;3) cards in your draw pile.\n| GivesToPlayer = Energy\n}}\n{{C|Aggregate}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' for every 4 (3 if upgraded) cards in your draw pile. If the amount of cards in your draw pile is not divisible by this number, it will be rounded down.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Aggregate card buffed. Energy gained every 6 -> 4 cards.\n** Aggregate+ card buffed. Energy gained every 5 -> 3 cards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 29: TURBO'''\n** Aggregate now gives the correct amount of energy.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2027":{"pageid":2027,"ns":0,"title":"Blur","revisions":[{"revid":56906,"parentid":55662,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Blur\n|Image       = Green-Blur.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (5;8) {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Block}} is not removed at the start of your next turn.\n|GivesToPlayer = Block, Blur\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Blur\n|Image        = Icon Blur.png\n|Description  = {{KW|Block}} is not removed at the beginning of your next X turns.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Duration\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n|InteractsWith = Block\n}}\n{{C|Blur}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 {{KW|Block}} and 1 {{BD|Blur}}, which prevents your {{KW|Block}} from being removed in between that amount of turns. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Blur}} takes precedence over {{R|Calipers}}, effectively removing all effects of the relic for an amount of turns equal to your {{BD|Blur}}.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2111":{"pageid":2111,"ns":0,"title":"Capacitor","revisions":[{"revid":56926,"parentid":55682,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Capacitor\n|Image       = Blue-Capacitor.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (2;3) {{KW|Orb Slot|Orb slots}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Orb Slot\n}}\n{{Keyword_Infobox|Orb Slot}}\n{{C|Capacitor}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}. <!---When played, it adds 2 (3) {{KW|Orbs|Orb Slots}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* As {{BD|Storm}} happens after Capacitor resolves, if your Orb Slots are full beforehand the {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} will take the first slot added by Capacitor.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* More Orb slots increase the potential damage of {{C|Barrage}}.\n* {{C|Fission}} can be used for more draw and {{Icon|BE}} Energy, as well as {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} Orbs if {{C|Fission}} is upgraded.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws an additional card for each different type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}; more Orb Slots allows the maximum draw of 4 cards, as well as making it easier to keep multiple Orb types Channeled.\n* More Orb Slots may benefit all Orb generation sources, but especially ones which have the potential to fill slots quickly, such as {{C|Tempest}}, {{C|Chill}}, {{C|Glacier}}, {{C|Rainbow}}, and {{C|Electrodynamics}}.\n* {{C|Consume}} can be used more times with additional Orb Slots, allowing for large {{BD|Focus}} gain.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The maximum amount of Orb Slots is 10.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1968":{"pageid":1968,"ns":0,"title":"Corpse Explosion","revisions":[{"revid":56790,"parentid":56023,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Corpse Explosion\n|Image       = Green-CorpseExplosion.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Apply (6;9) {{BD|Poison}}.<br>When the enemy dies, deal damage equal to its max HP to ALL enemies.\n|GivesToEnemy = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Corpse Explosion\n|Image        = Icon CorpseExplosion.png\n|Description  = On death, deal damage equal to Max HP X times to ALL enemies.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{C|Corpse Explosion}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\nAs {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy's turn, it has some unusual interactions:\n* If the damage is enough to cause {{M|The Guardian}} to change to Defensive form, it will immediately change its [[Intent]] to apply {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Moreover, as it is already past the point in its turn where {{KW|Block}} is removed, it will keep the Block generated by moving to Defensive Form until its next turn.\n** Notably, in other cases where HP thresholds affect enemy [[Intent]] (such as {{M|The Champ}} and {{M|Time Eater}}), this happens on a subsequent turn, and will not be affected.\n* If the enemy dies to {{BD|Poison}}, the card drawn by {{R|Gremlin Horn}} will be held until your next turn.\n** Similarly, if a {{M|Bronze Orb}} dies while holding a card in Stasis, that card will be returned to you and stay in your hand until next turn.\n* If a {{M|Fungi Beast}} dies this way, you will receive {{BD|Vulnerable}} during the enemy turn, which may increase the amount of incoming damage for the turn.\n* If an enemy with {{BD|Minion|Minions}} dies this way, its Minions will still flee combat before attacking.\n\nCorpse Explosion applies the {{BD|Poison}}, then the {{BD|Corpse Explosion}} to the target. If the target has 1 stack of {{BD|Artifact}}, the {{BD|Corpse Explosion}} will go through.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Bane}} does additional damage if the target has {{BD|Poison}}.\n* {{C|Catalyst}} can double (triple) the amount of {{BD|Poison}} on a target.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} can be used in combats with multiple enemies to consolidate {{BD|Poison}} as enemies die.\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} applies 1 {{BD|Poison}} whenever this card applies {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n* {{C|Corpse Explosion}} works well with other sources of {{BD|Poison}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Deadly Poison}}, {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Envenom}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}}.\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Poison}} damage causes {{M|Lagavulin}} to wake up, consuming its Stunned turn in the process.\n* {{BD|Poison}} bypasses {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Flying}}.\n** The damage dealt by Corpse Explosion going off also bypasses Flight, but not {{KW|Block}}.\n* However, {{BD|Intangible}} reduces ''all'' sources of HP loss to 1, including {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will prevent applying {{BD|Poison}} and {{BD|Corpse Explosion}}.\n** However, as Corpse Explosion applies 2 [[Debuffs]] to the target for one card play, it can be very effective at clearing {{BD|Artifact}} for your other {{BD|Poison}} cards.\n* Certain bosses will remove all [[Debuffs]] during combat: {{M|The Champ}}, {{M|Awakened One}}, and {{M|Time Eater}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card is most likely a reference to the Diablo II Necromancer Corpse Explosion ability; in addition to have the exact same name, the mechanics of the card are also the same (deal damage to other enemies based on the health of the target)\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Adding beta art for Bane, Charge Battery, Fission, Choke, Corpse Explosion, and Equilibrium.\n** Fixed Corpse Explosion card's portrait using incorrect card type.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 35: Aggregate'''\n** Corpse Explosion power is now a debuff.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** Corpse Explosion power can now trigger on Darklings.\n** Updating Power icon for Corpse Explosion.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Rework: Corpse Explosion card: Apply 6 Poison. When this enemy dies, deal damage to ALL enemies equal to its max HP.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Corpse Explosion is now affected by Powers (Vulnerable, Strength, Pen Nib, etc)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Corpse Explosion card's type is now Attack.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1965":{"pageid":1965,"ns":0,"title":"Crippling Cloud","revisions":[{"revid":56784,"parentid":56038,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Crippling Cloud\n|Image       = Green-CripplingCloud.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Apply (4;7) {{BD|Poison}} and 2 {{BD|Weak}} to ALL enemies.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Poison, Weak\n|GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}} {{Power Infobox|Weak}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Crippling Cloud}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\nAs {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy's turn, it has some unusual interactions:\n* If the damage is enough to cause {{M|The Guardian}} to change to Defensive form, it will immediately change its [[Intent]] to apply {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Moreover, as it is already past the point in its turn where {{KW|Block}} is removed, it will keep the Block generated by moving to Defensive Form until its next turn.\n** Notably, in other cases where HP thresholds affect enemy [[Intent]] (such as {{M|The Champ}} and {{M|Time Eater}}), this happens on a subsequent turn, and will not be affected.\n* If the enemy dies to {{BD|Poison}}, the card drawn by {{R|Gremlin Horn}} will be held until your next turn.\n** Similarly, if a {{M|Bronze Orb}} dies while holding a card in Stasis, that card will be returned to you and stay in your hand until next turn.\n* If a {{M|Fungi Beast}} dies this way, you will receive {{BD|Vulnerable}} during the enemy turn, which may increase the amount of incoming damage for the turn.\n* If an enemy with {{BD|Minion|Minions}} dies this way, its Minions will still flee combat before attacking.\n\nCrippling Cloud applies the {{BD|Poison}}, then the {{BD|Weak}} to each enemy. If an enemy has 1 stack of {{BD|Artifact}}, the Weak will go through.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Krane}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Weak}}.\n* {{C|Bane}} does additional damage if the target has {{BD|Poison}}.\n* {{C|Catalyst}} can double (triple) the amount of {{BD|Poison}} on a target.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} can be used in combats with multiple enemies to consolidate {{BD|Poison}} as enemies die.\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} applies 1 {{BD|Poison}} whenever this card applies {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n* {{C|Crippling Cloud}} works well with other sources of {{BD|Poison}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Deadly Poison}}, {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}, {{C|Envenom}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}}.\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Poison}} damage causes {{M|Lagavulin}} to wake up, consuming its Stunned turn in the process.\n* {{BD|Poison}} bypasses {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Flying}}.\n* However, {{BD|Intangible}} reduces ''all'' sources of HP loss to 1, including {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will prevent applying {{BD|Poison}} and {{BD|Weak}}.\n** However, as Crippling Cloud applies 2 [[Debuffs]] to all enemies for one card play, it can be very effective at clearing {{BD|Artifact}} for your other {{BD|Poison}} cards.\n* Certain bosses will remove all [[Debuffs]] during combat: {{M|The Champ}}, {{M|Awakened One}}, and {{M|Time Eater}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Crippling Poison rework: Apply 4 (7) Poison and 2 Weak to ALL enemies. Exhaust.\n** Crippling Poison -> Crippling Cloud.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Card Crippling Poison+ gets buffed from 4 -> 5 Poison & Weak.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2046":{"pageid":2046,"ns":0,"title":"Escape Plan","revisions":[{"revid":55763,"parentid":50505,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Escape Plan\n|Image       = Green-EscapePlan.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Draw 1 card.<br>If you draw a Skill, gain (3;5) {{KW|Block}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Escape Plan}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 1 card. If the card drawn that way was a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}, gain 3 (5 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|No Draw}} from {{C|Bullet Time}} or {{C|Battle Trance}} will prevent this card from drawing anything, meaning it also prevents this card from giving {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Escape Plan gaining Block when card drawn is blocked by No Draw power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Capitalizing the word 'Skill' for Escape Plan's description.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1895":{"pageid":1895,"ns":0,"title":"Exhume","revisions":[{"revid":56429,"parentid":50459,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Exhume\n| Image       = Red-Exhume.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = Put a card from your {{KW|Exhaust}} pile into your hand.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n| InteractsWith = Ehxaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Exhume}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It puts a previously {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} card back in your hand. {{C|Exhume}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergy ===\n* As {{C|Exhume}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} itself and gives back another card which was already {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}, it has {{KW|Exhaust}}-synergy with {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{R|Charon's Ashes}}, and {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n\n* {{C|Exhume}} is most useful for its flexibity, as it can allow an additional play of any card that was previously {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}, effectively acting as a copy of whatever {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} card is most useful at the time.\n** In the case of cards that scale themselves, such as {{C|Ritual Dagger}} or {{C|Rampage}}, {{C|Exhume}} is better than a second copy of that card, as it allows you to benefit from the previous scaling of that card, and scale that exact same card again.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Exhume}} cannot be used to put another {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} {{C|Exhume}} back in your hand.\n** This is done to prevent degenerate strategies that would be too easy to create an infinite damage combo. For example, by repeatedly using {{C|Exhume}}+ to bring back another {{C|Exhume}}+ and infinitely trigger the damage from {{R|Letter Opener}} without spending any {{KW|Energy}} or needing to draw cards.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card is the only way to bring back an {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} card. \n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 19: Seed'''\n** Put vs Place wording inconsistency on Thinking Ahead and Exhume cards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Exhume card can no longer return an Exhume card to your hand.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2050":{"pageid":2050,"ns":0,"title":"Expertise","revisions":[{"revid":50509,"parentid":36318,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Expertise\n|Image       = Green-Expertise.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Draw cards until you have (6;7) in your hand.\n|Keywords    = Draw, Hand\n}}\n{{C|Expertise}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws cards until you have 6 (7 if upgraded) cards in your hand. If you already have more than that amount of cards in hand when playing this card, it will have no effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The {{C|Expertise}} is removed from your hand ''before'' it takes effect, meaning it does not count towards the amount of cards in hand for the purposes of its own effect.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Expertise+ card nerf: 8 -> 7 cards in hand.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 11: A Library of Features'''\n** New Green card: Expertise\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2319":{"pageid":2319,"ns":0,"title":"Flash of Steel","revisions":[{"revid":50726,"parentid":36927,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Flash of Steel\n|Image       = Colorless-FlashofSteel.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (3;6) damage.<br>Draw 1 card.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Flash of Steel}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 3 (6 if upgraded) damage, and draws 1 card.\n\n== Obtaining Flash of Steel ==\n{{C|Flash of Steel}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Flash Of Steel+. 3 -> 6 damage.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1839":{"pageid":1839,"ns":0,"title":"Iron Wave","revisions":[{"revid":56390,"parentid":55830,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Iron Wave\n| Image       = Red-IronWave.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (5;7) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Deal (5;7) damage.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Iron Wave}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It gives 5 (7 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and deals 5 (7 if upgraded) damage.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} is gained before the damage is dealt or the card is resolved, meaning the {{KW|Block}} already protects from any damage sustained as a result of playing this card through effects like:\n** {{BD|Sharp Hide}} or {{BD|Thorns}}.\n** {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Both values are affected separately by effects that change the amount of damage and {{KW|Block}}, such as {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2017":{"pageid":2017,"ns":0,"title":"Leap","revisions":[{"revid":56791,"parentid":50563,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Leap\n|Image       = Blue-Leap.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (9;12) {{KW|Block}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Leap}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] is a Super Mario Bros. reference.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\nThis week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\nA new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2056":{"pageid":2056,"ns":0,"title":"Leg Sweep","revisions":[{"revid":55836,"parentid":50515,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Leg Sweep\n|Image       = Green-LegSweep.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Apply (2;3) {{BD|Weak}}.<br>Gain (11;14) {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}{{C|Leg Sweep}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 11 (14 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and applies 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Krane}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Leg Sweep card nerf: 12 -> 11 Block. Leg Sweep+ nerf: 15 -> 14 Block.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2041":{"pageid":2041,"ns":0,"title":"Malaise","revisions":[{"revid":55850,"parentid":50538,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Malaise\n|Image       = Green-Malaise.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Enemy loses (X;X+1) {{BD|Strength}}. Apply (X;X+1) {{BD|Weak}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}} {{Power Infobox|Weak}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Malaise}} is an X {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives '''negative''' X (X+1 if upgraded) {{BD|Strength}} and applies X (X+1 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}} to the target. {{C|Malaise}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\nWhen playing an X {{Icon|GE}}-cost card, all {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' that you currently have will be consumed. The {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' consumed this way will be used as the value for X.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Krane}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Weak}}.\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Malaise}} apply 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}} or {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Malaise}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of X will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Malaise}} can be targeted by {{C|Recycle}} to double the current {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Malaise increased in rarity (Uncommon-Rare).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Removing 'Spend all [R].' from all X-cost cards for consistency.\n** Fixed bug where cost X cards do not work with energy gain cards if played too fast.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2454":{"pageid":2454,"ns":0,"title":"Metamorphosis","revisions":[{"revid":55860,"parentid":55464,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Metamorphosis\n|Image       = Colorless-Metamorphosis.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Shuffle (3;5) random Attacks into your draw pile. They cost 0 this combat.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Metamorphosis}} is a 2 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It shuffles 3 (5 if upgraded) random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards into your draw pile, which will have their normal cost replaced by 0 for this combat, after which this {{C|Metamorphosis}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. \n\n{{C|Metamorphosis}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n\n== Obtaining Metamorphosis ==\n{{C|Metamorphosis}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* The randomization of {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}} will override the cost of the cards generated by this card.\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Feed}}\n* {{C|Reaper}}\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}}\n* {{C|Bite}}\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}}\n* {{C|Shiv}}\n* {{C|Smite}}\n* {{C|Through Violence}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like  Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Metamorphosis.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1791":{"pageid":1791,"ns":0,"title":"Sneaky Strike","revisions":[{"revid":56361,"parentid":55946,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Sneaky Strike\n| Image       = Green-SneakyStrike.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (12;16) damage.<br>If you have discarded a card this turn,<br>gain {{Icon|GE}} {{Icon|GE}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Energy\n| InteractsWith = Discard\n}}\n{{C|Sneaky Strike}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 (16 if upgraded) damage. If you have [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] before playing this card in the same turn, gain 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Necronomicon}} will cause the player to gain 2 {{Icon|GE}} Energy twice if a card has already been discarded and {{C|Sneaky Strike}} is the first 2-cost card played that turn.\n\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n* Regardless of when it is drawn {{C|Sneaky Strike}}'s {{Icon|GE}} Energy-gain mechanic can be triggered if anything has previously been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] in the same turn, in one of the following ways:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Survivor}}, {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Dagger Throw}}, {{C|Prepared}}, {{C|Concentrate}}, {{C|Tools of the Trade}}, {{C|Unload}}.\n* {{C|All-Out Attack}}, although this risks discarding {{C|Sneaky Strike}}.\n* {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, if {{C|Sneaky Strike}} is drawn after playing it.\n* {{C|Storm of Steel}}, if {{C|Sneaky Strike}} is drawn after playing it, such as with {{R|Unceasing Top}} or {{C|Reflex}}.\n* {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Gambling Chip}}.\n* {{P|Gambler's Brew}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* No matter what {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{C|Sneaky Strike}} has, the player will always gain 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if it is played after a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] previously that turn. This can be used to your advantage by reducing the cost below 2, but can lose you {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' as well if the cost is increased to 3:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Setup}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain, although this extra energy is often useless.\n* {{C|Enlightenment}} sets the cost to 1, resulting in 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{C|Madness}} sets the cost to 0, resulting in 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* If {{C|Sneaky Strike}} is selected from an {{P|Attack Potion}} it will have a cost of 0, resulting in 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' gain.\n* {{BD|Confused}} and {{P|Snecko Oil}} will randomize the cost from 0 to 3, which can result in a neutral, gained or lost amount of energy.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows a drawing of a bowling strike, as opposed to the physical action of striking someone.\n** This could mean the [[Silent]] is actually great at bowling which could have serious lore implications.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Sneaky Strike card buffed. Damage increased from 10 -> 12.\n** Sneaky Strike+ card buffed. Damage increased from 14 -> 16.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Sneaky Strike card buff. 8 -> 10 damage. Upgraded: 12 -> 14 damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Underhand Strike is now called Sneaky Strike.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 16: Back to Work'''\n** Underhanded Strike card rework: Cost 2: Deal 8 damage. If you have discarded a card this turn, gain 2 Energy.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** We removed one level of unlocks! Three additional cards are now available by default in the card pool for both The Silent and Ironclad. The following cards are now added to the card pool by default: Underhanded Strike, Reflex, Tactician\n\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2439":{"pageid":2439,"ns":0,"title":"Trip","revisions":[{"revid":55985,"parentid":50738,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Trip\n|Image       = Colorless-Trip.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Apply 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}(; to ALL enemies).\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}\n{{C|Trip}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It applies 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}} to the target, or to '''ALL''' enemies if upgraded.\n\n== Obtaining Trip ==\n{{C|Trip}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows the {{M|Bronze Automaton}} falling over. Unfortunately, this is not what happens if you play {{C|Trip}} on it.\n<!-- False advertising smh my head. -->\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Trip can now upgrade (Single Target -> All enemies)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Trip card buffed.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2312":{"pageid":2312,"ns":0,"title":"Weave","revisions":[{"revid":54868,"parentid":50688,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Weave\n|Image       = Purple-Weave.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (4;6) damage.<br>Whenever you {{KW|Scry}}, return this from the discard pile to your hand.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Scry}}\n{{C|Weave}} is a 0 {{Icon|PE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 (6 if upgraded) damage. If it is in your discard pile when you {{KW|Scry}}, it will be placed into your hand, if there is space in your hand.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* When {{KW|Scry|Scrying}}, any {{C|Weave}} only gets added into your hand after the {{KW|Scry|Scrying}} is resolved. This means that if {{C|Weave}} is moved to the discard pile as a result of {{KW|Scry|Scrying}}, it will be placed into your hand immediately.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Uniquely, {{C|Weave}} (and the similar card {{C|Flurry of Blows}}) are beneficial to have in your discard pile. This means they synergize well with effects that can place it there, such as {{KW|Scry}} and [[Keywords#Discard|Discard]].\n* Anything that can cause you to {{KW|Scry}} will synergize with this card:\n** {{C|Cut Through Fate}}\n** {{C|Third Eye}}\n** {{C|Foresight}} will trigger it at the start of every turn.\n** {{R|Melange}} will trigger this whenever you shuffle your draw pile.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1884":{"pageid":1884,"ns":0,"title":"Whirlwind","revisions":[{"revid":56002,"parentid":50450,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Whirlwind\n|Image       = Red-Whirlwind.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Deal (5;8) damage to ALL enemies X times.\n}}\n{{C|Whirlwind}} is an X {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (8 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies X times.\n\nWhen playing an X {{Icon|RE}}-cost card, all {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' that you currently have will be consumed. The {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' consumed this way will be used as the value for X.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits X times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Whirlwind}} hit 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If {{C|Whirlwind}} is used with 2 or more {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''', it will be able to trigger {{R|Necronomicon}}.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}}, {{R|Nunchaku}}, {{R|Kunai}}, {{R|Shuriken}}, and {{R|Ornamental Fan}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Whirlwind}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Double Tap}}, the value of X will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Whirlwind}} can be targeted by {{C|Recycle}} to double the current {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|All for One}} or {{C|Scrape}}, even with {{C|Swivel}}'s {{BD|Free Attack Power}} active.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Adding VFX for Whirlwind card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Adding SFX for Whirlwind card + Guardian enemy.\n** Updating SFX for Whirlwind (card AND Guardian enemy).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Whirlwind card gets an additional SFX.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** Fixed issue where playing cost X cards quickly after energy gain cards failed. Offering -> Whirlwind\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Removing 'Spend all [R].' from all X-cost cards for consistency.\n** Fixed bug where cost X cards do not work with energy gain cards if played too fast.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2323":{"pageid":2323,"ns":0,"title":"Wound","revisions":[{"revid":56004,"parentid":50790,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Wound\n|Image       = Colorless-Wound.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Status\n|Rarity      = Status\n|Cost        = -2\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Wound}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} Card.\n\n== Obtaining Wound ==\n\n* {{C|Wild Strike}} adds a Wound to the player's draw pile.\n* {{C|Power Through}} adds 2 Wounds to the player's hand. If one or more Wounds can't fit in the player's hand (i.e. they have 9 or 10 cards in hand already), the extra Wound(s) are added to the discard pile instead.\n* {{R|Mark of Pain}} adds 2 Wounds to the player's draw pile after they've finished drawing their opening hand for the start of combat.\n\nThe following enemies can give the player Wounds:\n* {{M|Book of Stabbing}}\n** {{BD|Painful Stabs}} - Whenever you receive attack damage from this enemy, add a {{C|Wound}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Taskmaster}}\n** {{Int|Taskmaster|Scouring Whip}} - Adds 1({{Asc|3|2}} | {{Asc|18|3}}) {{C|Wound|Wounds}} into your draw pile.\n* {{M|Dagger}}\n** {{Int|Dagger|Wound}} - Adds a {{C|Wound}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Corrupt Heart}}\n** Gains {{BD|Painful Stabs}} every 5th time using {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Buff}} starting at the 3rd use.\n** {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Debilitate}} - Adds 1 {{C|Wound}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Mark of Pain}} adds 2 Wounds to the player's draw pile after they've finished drawing their normal 5-card opening hand for the start of combat.\n** These Wounds '''can''' still end up in the opening hand due to {{R|Bag of Preparation}} drawing extra cards at the start of combat, as long as it was picked up after already having obtained {{R|Mark of Pain}} earlier.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Triggers the damage from {{C|Fire Breathing}}.\n* Draws cards with {{C|Evolve}}.\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} by {{C|Second Wind}} and triggers its {{KW|Block}} gain.\n* Can be {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} with {{R|Medical Kit}} to trigger exhaust synergies such as {{C|Feel No Pain}} or {{R|Charon's Ashes}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} by {{C|Sever Soul}} since it's not an {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|Attack}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Prevents {{C|Clash}} from being played.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows the [[Silent]] having a very understandable reaction to a minor cut.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}